    <string name="disclosure_title">How Imaa uses Accessibility</string>
    <string name="disclosure_body">Imaa is an accessibility tool for hands-free control. When you turn it on, Imaa can:\n\n• perform taps, swipes and pinches you ask for with gestures (scroll, zoom, next/previous),\n• press system buttons (Back, Home, Recents, Notifications, Screenshot),\n• look for a visible “Skip ad” button on screen and press it when you make the skip gesture.\n\nImaa does not read, store or send your screen content, typing or personal data. Everything stays on this phone. You can turn it off at any time in Settings → Accessibility.</string>
    <string name="disclosure_agree">I agree, open settings</string>
    <string name="disclosure_cancel">Not now</string>
    <string name="camera_permission">Imaa needs the camera to see your gestures. The picture never leaves your phone.</string>
